Facility
-refers to buildings, equipment, services, or a combination of these that are designed or equipped to serve a particular purpose


Concerning Facilities
-Facilities must be adequately illuminated, clean neat, and dry.
-Keep the area organized so that there are no obstacles lying around on the floor.
-The equipment and the floor area around the equipment must be free from dust and chipping.



Maintenance
-an excellent means of improving the performance and condition of equipment and facilities

How to Maintain (5Ms)
-Manpower
-Money (Financial Resources)
-Methods and Systems
-Machines (Facilities)
-Materials and Supplies


Maintenance Program
-It is a comprehensive list of maintenance and its incidents which includes the following:
  >Maintenance activities to be undertakes
  >Manpower needed
  >Maintenance methods to be used
  >Supplies and Materials needed for the maintenance
  >Cost involved in the maintenance


What, When, Where?
-What routine actions must be done to keep the device on working order
-Where is the maintenance to be carried out
-When do you perform the maintenance activities


Maintenance Schedule
- a list of allocating specific maintenance of an area
- This is just part of maintenance program


Maintenance Checklist
- List of maintenance tasks (predictive or preventive) typically derived from some form of analysis, 
    generated automatically as work orders at pre-determined frequency.



5S - Sort, Shine, Set in order, Sustain, Standardize

Safety - new addition to 5S
-The freedom from danger, injury or damage
-Ways to learn and understand safety

Accidental Experiences
-Safety Education is a means of developing awareness of the dangers inherent in a situation, thus enabling
  the learner to avoid or minimize corresponding injuries.


SAfety in Maintaining Training Facilities
This includes the following:
-Regularly checking equipment for defects,
-Keeping the training area clean and organized
-Ensuring proper storage of tools, materials
-Following safety signs and rules

Hazardous materials should be properly labeled and stored, while faulty equipment must be reported and repaired immediately



Breakdown
- A breakdown is the failure or mechanical failure of a machine causing to stop operating.
- To stop functioning due to wear, damage, or malfunction

Partial breakdown
- The vehicle is still functional but limited operation, or continued operation could cause further damage.

Salvage
-the act of saving or recovering value of property that has been destroyed , damaged, or abandoned.
-the rescue of property from peril or the recovery of value from waste or damaged materials
-(Context) In the insurance industry, it occurs when a vahicle is declared a "total loss" (uneconomical repair)
-Types of Salvage can be Repaired  or Used for Parts.


Hierarchy of Waste
(top to bottom): Prevention - Minimisation - Re-use - Recycling - Energy Recovery - Disposal
(Reduce - Re-use - Recycle)



Occupational Health and Safety 
-it is a cross-disciplinary area concerned with protecting the safety health and welfare of people
engaged in work or employment

